          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            inputs, we can define a
            %strong multimorphism of algebras
            in the same way.
          %p We can view a binary morphism as a morphism which is a “morphism of algebras in each variable separately”. This intuition can be made precise as follows.
          #bimorphs.num_theorem
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Kock71bilin"}> Kock ‘71, Theorem 1.1
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Seal12"} Seal ‘12, Proposition 2.1.2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\otimes B\to R
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a binary morphism of algebras if and only if both the following two diagrams commute. (The maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              denote the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strength and costrength
              of the monad
