            with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
            extending its usual category structure. The most prominent example of this is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+maps"} multilinear maps
            extending
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
          %p As in the case of multilinear maps, we have that the tensor product of algebras, if it exists, represent multimorphisms.
          #uniprop.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Seal12"}> Seal ‘12, Proposition 2.3.4
