            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategory"} representable multicategory
          %p The proof (see the reference above) follows closely the classical case of modules over a ring.
          %h2#for_monoidal_closed_categories For monoidal closed categories
          %p
            The treatment of the closed case goes back to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Kock71closed"} the work done in the 70s by Anders Kock
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Brandenburg2014"} the thesis of Martin Brandenburg
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+closed+category"} monoidal closed category
            and has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^T
            has tensors, the first hypothesis of
            %a{:href => "#sealthms"} the theorem above
            is satisfied, and so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C^T,\otimes_T,T1)
            is a monoidal category. Moreover,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^T
            can be equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
